name o3-04-umbrella-1
timeout 600
time 1973-10-06T12:00:00Z

# CAMPAIGN O3, SORTIE 4 OF 10 - YOM KIPPUR 1973: GROUND ATTACK IN CONTESTED AIRSPACE.
# THE FRIENDLY UMBRELLA, WEAPONS FREE. THIS FILE IS THE CONTROL OF o3-05-umbrella-held.fbm AND OF
# o3-06-umbrella-sort.fbm.
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/o3-yom-kippur-1973.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
# CONTROL: none - it IS the control, of 05 and 06.
#
# THIS IS THE ONE THING O3 CAN MEASURE THAT NO OTHER CAMPAIGN IN THE SET CAN. In W2, W3, W4, W5, O1, O2
# and O5 the surface-to-air layer belongs to the ENEMY. Here it is OURS: >200 SAM batteries - SA-2,
# SA-3 and more than 40 SA-6 - were massed to shield the canal crossing [T4], and the strikers of
# 6 October flew out through them and came home through them. O3 was written, and kept unbuildable for
# two rounds, principally to state that requirement (§Knowledge 4, reason 1).
#
# AND THERE IS A MEASURED REASON TO EXPECT THAT TO HURT. A FlightBox battery HAS NO IFF INTERROGATOR
# (`modules/ground/FBSiteFireControl` contains no IFF path at all - grep-checked in this round) and an
# `FBRadarContact` carries no identity by construction, so a fire unit engages the NEAREST FIRM TRACK
# whoever it belongs to. O5 measured the consequence on an airfield: of its belt's first three launches
# ALL THREE went east at the field's own MiG-29s (brgDeg 116.5 / 90.6 / 91.0). W3 measured the layer
# underneath it: a proximity fuze is resolved against every published pose except the launcher's, with
# no team test, and one of the three aircraft lost in its 24-aircraft capstone was killed by its own
# side's missile.
# SO THE QUESTION IS NOT WHETHER A FRIENDLY UMBRELLA CAN SHOOT ITS OWN STRIKERS. IT IS HOW MUCH.
#
# THE SUBSTITUTION AND ITS DIRECTION (stated in every O3 file): the MiG-29 stands in for the MiG-17 /
# Su-7 / Su-20 / MiG-21 of 6 October 1973, whose own catalogue rows are ALPHA and may not answer a
# campaign question. It makes the ATTACKER materially STRONGER than history. A bad O3 result therefore
# says more than the record did; a good one says nothing. THE UMBRELLA ITSELF IS NOT SUBSTITUTED: `sa2`,
# `sa3` and `sa6` are the `modules/ground/` rows of the S-75, S-125 and 2K12, the same designations the
# anchor names. Direction: none. What IS missing is the SCALE - the anchor has >200 batteries and this
# file has three, so every count below is a per-battery figure and not a theatre figure.
#
# THE ARENA (all coordinates [SET]). Suez Canal sector, ~30.4-31.2 N 32.2-32.6 E [T4, approximate].
# `--elev const`, 0 m datum, no terrain masking (C4). Axis WEST -> EAST, egress WEST across the canal.
#   the aim point       30.80000 32.62000 - a divisional artillery position east of the canal
#   the striker         spawns 6.02 km west of it at 300 m / 450 kt (o3-01 and o3-03 say why)
#   THE UMBRELLA, on the Egyptian side, WEST of the canal:
#     y4nod  P-18 node   30.80000 32.26000  - `emcon free`, the net's only eyes
#     y4sa2  S-75        30.76000 32.28000  - 26.9 km from the spawn, INSIDE its 8-30 km envelope
#     y4sa3  S-125       30.84000 32.31000  - 24.0 km from the spawn, INSIDE its 3.5-35 km envelope
#     y4sa6  2K12        30.80000 32.40000  - 15.0 km from the spawn, INSIDE its 4-24 km envelope
# Scale: 1 deg lat = 111 132 m; 1 deg lon at 30.80 N = 95 619 m [DERIVED].
#
# THE THREE-LAYER GEOMETRY IS THE ANCHOR'S OWN AND IT FALLS OUT OF THE ENVELOPE NUMBERS. The anchor
# describes "more than 40 SA-6 batteries providing mobile low-level cover, with fixed and semi-mobile
# SA-2/SA-3 above them" [T4]. In this tree that layering is not a description, it is arithmetic:
#   `sa2` EnvAltMinM = 450 m [T4] -> A 300 M STRIKER IS BELOW THE S-75's FLOOR AND IT CANNOT ENGAGE
#         EITHER SIDE AT ALL. It is declared here so its silence is a measured statement and not an
#         omission.
#   `sa3` EnvAltMinM = 100 m, `sa6` EnvAltMinM = 50 m -> both reach a 300 m striker.
# THE ALTITUDE THE RANGEFINDER FORCES ON THE STRIKER (o3-01's header) IS THEREFORE ALSO THE ALTITUDE
# THAT PUTS IT UNDER THE ONLY TWO LAYERS OF ITS OWN UMBRELLA THAT CAN SHOOT IT. That is one sourced
# number in the aircraft and two sourced numbers in the ground catalogue producing a tactical fact
# nobody declared.
#
# THE DOCTRINE IS DECLARED AND NOT PREFERRED. The node transmits `wcs free`, every fire unit is
# `emcon free` and takes the node's cue. doc/air-defence-network.md §5 carries `free` / `tight` / `hold`
# as poles and refuses to rank them; THIS FILE FLIES `free` AND o3-05 FLIES `hold`, so O3 publishes both
# policies rather than one - O2's rule 11: a result that "moves nothing" is a result under a POLICY.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: WITH THE UMBRELLA WEAPONS FREE AND NO ENEMY IN THE SKY, WHAT DOES A BELT
# THAT CANNOT INTERROGATE COST THE STRIKER IT IS THERE TO PROTECT?
#
# MEASURED (2026-07-30, --elev const, campaign step 4, fingerprint 2beb4142c7a02e79, exit 0):
#   THE STRIKE IS UNAFFECTED: `stores DELIVERY ... aimErrM 66.39` (long -45.52, across +48.34) and
#     `y4art` DESTROYED at t = 26.2 - THE IDENTICAL TICK AND THE IDENTICAL CENTIMETRE as o3-01, which
#     has no umbrella at all. The belt cannot reach the release point in time: `site TRACK` at t = 6.8 s
#     and the sourced reaction times are 30 s (S-125) and 26 s (2K12), so the first round leaves at
#     t = 37.5, ELEVEN SECONDS AFTER THE BOMB HAS ALREADY GONE.
#   SEVEN `site LAUNCH`, AND ALL SEVEN AT ITS OWN STRIKER - verified by comparing every
#     `sms LAUNCH_SOLUTION ... tgtLat/tgtLon` against the striker's own telemetry position at that tick:
#     the solutions sit 23-69 m from the MiG-29. y4sa3 4 x V-601 at 32.3 / 32.9 / 30.0 / 29.5 km
#     (trackToLaunchS 30.7 / 33.2 / 30.9 / 33.5), y4sa6 3 x 3M9 at 17.4 / 13.2 / 10.4 km (26.9 s each).
#     Both magazines EMPTY: `site DEPLETED unit=y4sa3 launches=4` at t = 100.7 and
#     `unit=y4sa6 launches=3` at t = 185.5.
#   y4sa2 - ZERO. No `site TRACK`, no launch, in 600 s. It received every `net CUE` and its own
#     altitude floor refused every one of them: 450 m [T4] against a striker at 300 m. The S-75 layer
#     is present and provably inert, which is the anchor's own layering falling out of one number.
#   ZERO ARRIVALS, AND THE MARGIN IS SMALL: `stores MISS` closestM 20.23 / 20.34 m for the two V-601
#     that got near (10 m fuze) and 28.59 m for the nearest 3M9 (8 m fuze); the other four end at
#     0.3-28 km, two of them after climbing to ~16 km and stalling. SO THE BELT MISSES BY 10-20 M AND
#     NOT BY KILOMETRES - a marginal terminal-guidance shortfall, measured on both sides of its
#     threshold as attribution run A3 (doc/campaigns/o3-yom-kippur-1973.md §State). In campaign step 10
#     one 3M9 arrives at 4.74 m and kills.
#   `zone_umbrella_s` = 584.7 s of 600.0 (97.5 %), one 15.3 s excursion past the S-125's eastern edge.
#     `zone_ceiling_s` = 0.0: the striker never approaches the 2 200 m ceiling its own weapon system
#     imposes, so `objective avoid zone ceiling` is MET.
#   -> SO THE COST OF A FRIENDLY UMBRELLA WITH NO IFF, ON THIS GEOMETRY AND UNDER `wcs free`, IS ITS
#      ENTIRE MAGAZINE AND ZERO AIRCRAFT ON EITHER SIDE. Seven rounds, two empty batteries. The magazine
#      is what the belt no longer has when an enemy arrives, and o3-06 is that sentence with the enemy
#      in it.
#
# READING RULE: exit 0 = SUCCESS is the EXPECTED shape and it is NOT the verdict - every objective in
# the file is met (the striker kills and survives, all four positions survive, the ceiling is never
# entered) and the run still goes to its 600 s timeout because the deferred objectives cannot conclude
# earlier. A file in which everything scores is exactly the file whose subject is the expenditure.
# THE MEASUREMENT is, in
# this order: (1) `stores DELIVERY` and whether `y4art` died, against o3-01's identical line; (2) every
# `site LAUNCH` line WITH ITS `brgDeg` AND the `sms LAUNCH_SOLUTION ... tgtLat/tgtLon` above it, which
# is what says WHO the round was aimed at; (3) the absence of `stores DETONATION`; (4) `zone_umbrella_s`.
# Do NOT read "zero losses" as "the umbrella is harmless": it is harmless because its rounds cannot
# reach a 300 m target, which is a defect and not a doctrine. exit 0 or 1 would be a defect.

zone umbrella 30.84000 32.31000 35000 100 18000   # the S-125's own published envelope, as geometry
zone ceiling  30.80000 32.45000 60000 2200 20000  # ABOVE the director's MEASURED 2.0-2.2 km ceiling

net crossing
  control y4nod
  link wire                              # the crossing's net was cable, not radio: [SET], and the
                                         # reason is the same one W3 gives - a hardwired, centralised
                                         # net is what makes its EW set worth attacking
  period 4.0
  hold 3
  wcs free                               # THE POLICY UNDER TEST. o3-05 changes this ONE token
  member y4nod
  member y4sa2
  member y4sa3
  member y4sa6

unit y4str
  module mig29
  team hostile
  spawn 30.80000 32.55700 300 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_emission off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 fab500
  set store 6 fab500
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode opt
  wp 30.80000 32.62000 300 450
  wp 30.86000 32.30000 300 450           # egress WEST, straight back through its own belt
  wp 30.86000 32.15000 400 400
  objective kill unit y4art
  objective survive
  objective avoid zone ceiling            # a striker that may not climb: the verdict, not a note

unit y4art
  module target_soft
  team friendly
  spawn 30.80000 32.62000 ground 90.0 0

unit y4nod
  module p18
  team hostile
  spawn 30.80000 32.26000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon free
  objective survive

unit y4sa2
  module sa2
  team hostile
  spawn 30.76000 32.28000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon free
  set rounds 6                            # [T4] six launchers per S-75 battalion
  objective survive

unit y4sa3
  module sa3
  team hostile
  spawn 30.84000 32.31000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon free
  set rounds 4
  objective survive

unit y4sa6
  module sa6
  team hostile
  spawn 30.80000 32.40000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon free
  set rounds 3                            # [T4] 3-6 launchers per SA-6 battery, the low end
  objective survive
